Title: The Trail of Bells — Trailer
Credit: AudStories Original

SCENE 1

EXT. VILLAGE OUTSKIRTS - DHARAMVANA - DUSK

SFX: Mountain wind. Distant forest ambience — deep, 
airy. Gravel crunching slowly under three sets of 
footsteps. A car rolls to a stop.

Car door shuts.

Silence settles.

Then — far inside the forest — a single bell.

Faint. Metallic. Almost too soft to be real.

ARNAV
(to his friends, grinning)
Dharamvana Village.

Exactly what we came for.

SFX: Footsteps move forward onto the trail.

SCENE 2

EXT. FOREST TRAIL - CONTINUOUS

SFX: Forest ambience closes in. More enclosed 
now. Less sky.

RISHABH
(scanning)
This trail is used.

ARNAV
There's a village nearby.

RISHABH
(quiet, to himself)
No footprints though.

SFX: The bell rings again. Same distance. 
Same direction.

MANAS
(stopping)
It doesn't sound like it's coming 
from one place.

SFX: Forest ambience tightens. The bell rings — 
this time, behind them.

A long beat of silence.

ARNAV
(testing, half-smile)
Hello?

SFX: The bell rings immediately. Sharp. 
Centered. Close.

RISHABH
(flat)
That timing was not random.

MANAS
(whisper)
It's learning us.

SFX: Forest ambience drops to near silence.
Sub-bass pressure tone — barely felt,
more sensation than sound.

SCENE 3

SFX: Wind dies. Only Arnav's voice now,
close to the mic.

ARNAV (V.O.)
(to camera, hollow)
There's a trail behind Dharamvana.

Locals say it's cursed.

People hear bells at night...

(beat)

and follow them.

SFX: A bell rings — far right.
Another — far left.
Another — directly behind.

Not synchronized. Not echoes.

SCENE 4

MANAS (O.S.)
(calm, gentle, wrong)
You don't have to be scared.

SFX: Silence.

Then the bell rings exactly where 
Manas' voice came from.

RISHABH
(terrified whisper)
That wasn't him.

A beat.

RISHABH (CONT'D)
(low, firm)
We need to go back. Now.

SFX: Mid-sentence silence. Abrupt. Clean.

ARNAV
(after a long beat, barely a whisper)
Rishabh?

SFX: Nothing answers.

Not even the bell.

SFX: All remaining sound drops away.

Two full beats of complete silence.

Then — Arnav's voice. Alone. 
Stripped of everything.

ARNAV (CONT'D)
(hollow, barely above a whisper)
It's not calling us.

A breath.

It's keeping us.

SFX: Silence. Two full seconds. Exact.

Then —

A single bell.

Clear. Calm. Patient.

Not threatening.

Almost inviting.

NARRATOR
(low, unhurried)
The Trail of Bells.

An AudStories Original.

SFX: The bell rings once more —
as if answering the title itself.

FADE TO SILENCE.




